#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""Owner-operated diagnostic pilot of one historical month of catalogue synchronization (#246).

The harness measures the existing UC-009 run; it never imports anything itself. `start` launches
exactly one calendar month through the private management command `POST /actuator/cataloguesync`
(the documented break-glass/diagnostic trigger, so no product endpoint, session or CSRF is
involved) and leaves a detached monitor that samples bounded evidence until the run ends. The
monitor is not the synchronization worker: the run executes on the application's own thread,
PostgreSQL's `catalogue.synchronization_run` row is its truth, and stopping or losing the monitor
never stops the run. Nothing here restarts a run, launches another month, changes configuration
or scheduling, writes to PostgreSQL or reads a secret's content.

Evidence is written incrementally under `<evidence-root>/<YYYY-MM>/<execution-id>/` so a crash or
host restart keeps what was measured; `report` rebuilds the summary from whatever exists.
"""

